{
 "title": "Procedural shaders part 2: sand and a sky",
 "summary": "A procedural sand shader on a Suzanne (Ctrl+3 subdivision): three noise textures on Object coordinates at scales 500, 250 and 150 multiplied together (Mix set to Multiply, factors 1 and 0.5), through a bump into the normal and into the roughness, coloured by mixing cadmium yellow FDDA0D with dioxazine purple 5C3A93; the pink lamp made white. Then a Sky Texture in the world (sun size 5, elevation 100, rotation 90, altitude 5500 m, ozone 10, strength 0.1) over a new ground plane. Beyond the tutorial: the ground rolled into sand dunes with a Displace modifier and given the same sand.",
